<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!-- Overrides glance-appwidget's EMPTY placeholder style of the same name (verified
         against glance-appwidget-1.1.1.aar: `<style name="Glance.AppWidget.List"
         parent=""/>`, referenced as style="@style/Glance.AppWidget.List" by every
         glance_list*.xml layout the LazyColumn translates to). App resources win the
         merge, and RemoteViews inflate with THIS package's resources inside the
         launcher, so the widget's ListView picks it up at inflate time.

         Why: the list's vertical scrollbar drew on top of the feed rows' right edge
         (round 2 device feedback #5 — Fred's red-box screenshot). RemoteViews exposes no
         setter for it and Glance no modifier, so the honest options were this style hook
         or a reserved gutter; the hook actually removes the bar instead of budgeting
         pixels around it. Failure mode is safe: if a Glance upgrade renames the style,
         this override goes inert and the scrollbar comes back — visible in the first
         gallery run, not a crash.

         tools:override marks the shadowing of the library's private style as deliberate
         (silences PrivateResource); UnusedResources is a false positive — no app code
         references the style, the glance layouts do, across a boundary lint cannot see. -->
    <style name="Glance.AppWidget.List" parent="" tools:override="true"
        tools:ignore="UnusedResources">
        <item name="android:scrollbars">none</item>
    </style>
</resources>
